clumppling
----------

gt_clumppling() implements the method of clumppling (Liu, Kopelman and
Rosenberg 2024), and its R and C++ code (R/gt_clumppling.R,
R/clumppling_*.R, src/clumppling_assignment.cpp) is ported, with
modifications, from the python package clumppling, version 2.0.10
(https://github.com/PopGenClustering/Clumppling), whose author is Xiran Liu.
The exceptions are the solver of the assignment problems (clumppling_lsap()
in src/clumppling_assignment.cpp; see "Hungarian algorithm" below), which
replaces clumppling's integer linear programs, and the community detection
methods ported from python-louvain and markov_clustering (below). The
critical values of its Tracy-Widom test (R/clumppling_community.R) are
those computed by clumppling, and the example data of gt_clumppling()
(inst/extdata/capeverde_admix.rds, inst/extdata/chicken_admix.rds and the
dataset capeverde_pops) are made from its example data. The plots of
gt_clumppling() (R/autoplot_gt_clumppling.R, R/plot_modes.R) follow the
design of clumppling's figures, but none of its plotting code is used.
